    Illustrative results based on a representative engagement; individual outcomes vary and are not guaranteed.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-4 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Why it mattered</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    Adding more staff would only have scaled the same manual bottleneck, not removed it. CMS Group didn't need more people reading documents faster &mdash; it needed the routine 85% of the work to stop requiring a person at all, so the people it already had could spend their time on the judgment calls that actually needed them.
  </p>
  <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-[#76B900] pl-4 text-[15px] italic leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">
    &ldquo;We didn't want to hire our way out of a process problem. We wanted the process fixed.&rdquo;
    <span class="mt-2 block not-italic text-[13px] text-navy-400">&mdash; Director of Operations, CMS Group</span>
  </blockquote>
</div>

<div class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-100/60 bg-white p-8 shadow-subtle" data-reveal>
  <blockquote class="mb-4 text-[19px] italic leading-relaxed text-[#111827]">
    &ldquo;Our team used to be the bottleneck between every document and the work that actually mattered. Now the routine 85% handles itself, and we only get involved when something genuinely needs a human look.&rdquo;
  </blockquote>
  <p class="text-[14px] text-[#6B7280]">
    <strong class="font-semibold text-[#111827]">Director of Operations</strong><br>
    CMS Group
  </p>
</div>

